    <section id="sect-00003">
      <title>Additional Resources</title>

      <section id="sect-00004">
        <title>Calculating and Interpreting Correlation Coefficients</title>
        <para id="para-00024">Properties of the correlation coefficient:</para>
        <list id="list-00001">
          <item>Property 1: The sign of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>r</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> (positive or negative) corresponds to the direction
            of the linear relationship.</item>
          <item>Property 2: A value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>r</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> indicates a perfect positive linear relationship,
            with all points in the scatter plot falling exactly on a straight line.</item>
          <item>Property 3: A value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>r</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> indicates a perfect negative linear relationship,
            with all points in the scatter plot falling exactly on a straight line.</item>
          <item>Property 4: The closer the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>r</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, the stronger the
            linear relationship.</item>
        </list>
        <para id="para-00025">Using the data of shoe length in inches and height in inches for 10 men, find the
          correlation coefficient of the data with graphing technology.</para>
        <table class="unnumbered os-raise-midsizetable unnumbered" id="table-00005">
          <tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<thead>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  <emphasis><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> (Shoe length) inches</emphasis>
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  <emphasis><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> (Height) inches</emphasis>
                </entry>
              </row>
              </thead>
